WEBVTT

00:10:29.166 --> 00:10:30.709
As Philip once said to me,

00:10:30.751 --> 00:10:33.045
"It's kind of like learning
how to ride a bike.

00:10:33.087 --> 00:10:35.714
It takes a bit of practice,
but once you're rolling,

00:10:35.714 --> 00:10:37.383
it becomes natural.

00:10:37.424 --> 00:10:41.261
Now I just look on the screen
where I want to click and I'm texting,

00:10:41.303 --> 00:10:43.013
messaging the world via Twitter."

00:10:43.013 --> 00:10:44.932
But Graham,

00:10:44.973 --> 00:10:47.643
he said, as his ALS was progressing,

00:10:47.685 --> 00:10:52.314
that it gave him immense comfort
to know that even if his body was failing,

00:10:52.356 --> 00:10:55.609
he was always going to be able
to tell his wife that he loved her.

00:10:59.029 --> 00:11:00.489
In the future,